---
title: Asynchronous usage accounting and monthly spend status
config:
  sequence:
    mirrorActors: false
---
%% Status uses exact original-month gross before credit and excludes add-ons.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C as Customer
    participant P as Sandbox platform
    participant A as Go billing API
    participant W as Go usage worker
    participant D as PostgreSQL
    Note over C,D: Row selector: customer_billing_state.customer_id = C<br/>Event row: usage_inbox.source = S and usage_inbox.event_id = E<br/>Request advisory identity: api_idempotency_operations.operation_scope<br/>plus api_idempotency_operations.idempotency_key (not a row lock)

    Note over A,D: Cyberdyne has a USD 15.00 monthly limit.<br/>This example reads status after each worker commit.
    P->>A: POST /usage/batches with first October usage
    A->>D: Commit usage_inbox usage_inbox rows
    A-->>P: 202 accepted<br/>no spend status in this response
    W->>D: Account usage_inbox row atomically<br/>October gross USD 6.17283945
    D-->>W: Committed monthly_usage and account state_version
    P->>A: GET /customers/cyberdyne/limit-status
    A->>D: Read current UTC month gross and customer_billing_state
    D-->>A: Exact gross, limit and version
    A-->>P: Exact October gross USD 6.17283945<br/>limit_reached false

    P->>A: POST /usage/batches for another USD 12.00 October charge
    A->>D: Commit usage_inbox usage_inbox rows
    A-->>P: 202 accepted
    W->>D: Commit October gross USD 18.17283945 and new state_version
    P->>A: GET /customers/cyberdyne/limit-status
    A->>D: Read committed October gross, limit and version
    A-->>P: Exact October gross USD 18.17283945<br/>limit_reached true
    Note over P: The platform decides how to enforce the limit.<br/>Billing retains all metered usage for invoicing.

    C->>A: POST /customers/cyberdyne/spend-limit<br/>New request key and limit_cents 2000
    A->>D: Scoped request lock<br/>account lock<br/>store limit and replay result
    A->>D: COMMIT api_idempotency_operations and incremented state_version
    A-->>C: 200 with the original request key and limit_cents 2000
    P->>A: GET /customers/cyberdyne/limit-status
    A->>D: Read October gross and the new limit
    A-->>P: October limit_reached false

    Note over P,D: November begins according to the server UTC clock.
    P->>A: GET /customers/cyberdyne/limit-status
    A->>D: Read November monthly_usage, or zero if no row exists
    D-->>A: USD 0.00<br/>monthly limit remains USD 20.00
    A-->>P: November limit_reached false
    Note over A,D: Reads can lag accepted inbox data while accounting is pending.<br/>Late October usage changes October gross, even if billed in November.<br/>New-month status needs no midnight cron<br/>snapshots identify month and version.
